From 051d7189e84deea2b0bab90c3dba6a480942ac7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMB-1 FM6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:31:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Each voice's patch edited operator by operator, DX7 banks
 over SysEx, five modulators a voice, MIDI CC

- VOICE, OPERATOR and MOD groups of pages for the pad, the bells and the bass: algorithm, feedback, LFO, pitch
  envelope; each operator's ratio, fine, level, envelope, mode, detune, velocity, key scaling, amp sensitivity
  (KNOB 1 picks the operator), heard at once on the sounding notes (fm6_note_refresh)
- each voice plays its own patch: its six, or a voice of the 16 DX7 banks in the flash (app/bank.c), sent from
  tools/amb_syx.py in 640-byte SysEx chunks; a DX7 single voice dump goes into the voice shown
- five modulators a voice, summed, with every target down to one operator's level, ratio, fine pitch and envelope,
  and LFO PM; every voice runs its patch's LFO
- MIDI CC and NRPN in and out (channel 16 the layers', 1..3 each voice's modulators and patch bytes)
- project format 7 (the pieces' patches in OBJ_PATCH); format 6's FM edits baked into the patch
- en_init resets the garden's randomness and transport, so a test hears A against B on the same notes

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
